description.narrative:
The overall goal is to prepare a baseline and the development of monitoring systems for the project "Guaranteeing the rights and defence of citizenship of indigenous peoples of the Middle Solimões River and Tributaries". This is an essential capacity strengthening activity to support CIMI and Caritas' to manage institutional funded projects. 
Main activities include: 
1. Project baseline: aims to develop the baseline that will guide the implementation of the project by providing the information for the construction of the monitoring system.
The consultant's activities consist of: preparation of questionnaires to be applied in a sample of the target audience of the project; training of the technicians of the project on the questionnaires; tabulation of data; preparation of the baseline report.
Products:
- 02 prepared questionnaires;
- Workshop for the questionnaires;
- Baseline Report

2. Monitoring System: aims to build the methodology, the tools and the process of monitoring the activities and results anticipated in the project. It also includes providing support (at a distance and face-to-face) to the staff of CIMI and Caritas Tefe.
The consultant activities consist of: developing the methodology for the monitoring of activities and results; workshop process and monitoring system; prepare the methodological guide for monitoring; develop instruments for recording information relating to the activities and results; develop tools for consolidation of data and information (monitoring matrix); prepare the necessary procedures for the drafting of activity reports (mid-year and annual); support the review, writing, and final editing of the reports; and constant support to the monitoring process.
Products:
- Methodological guide for the process and monitoring system;
- Activity registers;
- Workshop on monitoring systems and processes;
- Instruments for monitoring the target group;
- Activities centralisation spreadsheet;
- Mid-year and annual reports on activities and monitoring matrix;
